SUMMARY:Legally Blonde | Additional Films and Guests
DESCRIPTION:Elle Woods (Reese Witherspoon) is a California blonde with co
 uture clothes (mostly pink\, obvs)\, fabulous friends\, and the hottest b
 oyfriend on campus. So when Warner Huntington III (Matthew Davis) suddenl
 y dumps her and heads to Harvard Law School\, Elle takes matters into her
  own manicured hands and enrolls as well. Now\, getting Warner back shoul
 d be a snap (well\, maybe a bend and snap)\, right? Wrong! Elle's about t
 o begin the toughest fight of her life … for love\, honor\, justice\, a
 nd respect for blondes everywhere! Luke Wilson\, Selma Blair\, Victor Gar
 ber\, Holland Taylor\, and Jennifer Coolidge round out a fantastic ensemb
 le cast. [96 min\; comedy\, romantic comedy\, satire\; English]  The Leag
 ue of Women Voters is a nonpartisan political organization active at nati
 onal\, state\, and local levels that encourages informed participation in
  government. The local LWV table\, located outside the Cinema before the 
 screening\, will assist citizens to register to vote or check their regis
 tration\, and share how to obtain factual information on the ballots and 
 candidates.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Elle Woods (Reese Witherspoon) is a Cal
 ifornia blonde with couture clothes (mostly pink\, obvs)\, fabulous frien
 ds\, and the hottest boyfriend on campus. So when Warner Huntington III (
 Matthew Davis) suddenly dumps her and heads to Harvard Law School\, Elle 
 takes matters into her own manicured hands and enrolls as well. Now\, get
 ting Warner back should be a snap (well\, maybe a bend and snap)\, right?
  Wrong! Elle's about to begin the toughest fight of her life … for love
 \, honor\, justice\, and respect for blondes everywhere! Luke Wilson\, Se
 lma Blair\, Victor Garber\, Holland Taylor\, and Jennifer Coolidge round 
 out a fantastic ensemble cast. [96 min\; comedy\, romantic comedy\, satir
 e\; English]</p><p>  The League of Women Voters is a nonpartisan politica
 l organization active at national\, state\, and local levels that encoura
 ges informed participation in government. The local LWV table\, located o
 utside the Cinema before the screening\, will assist citizens to register
  to vote or check their registration\, and share how to obtain factual in
 formation on the ballots and candidates.</p>
