SUMMARY:Singles | Soundtracks of a Generation
DESCRIPTION:Arranged as an episodic comedy\, Singles spotlights the inter
 twined lives of the co-habitants\, friends\, and bandmates of the same Se
 attle apartment building. Foregrounded by the tumultuous romantic relatio
 nship between Steve (Campbell Scott) and Linda (Kyra Sedgwick)—who meet
  at an Alice in Chains concert\, of course!—the drama extends to their 
 friendship with Janet Livermore (Bridget Fonda)\, who is tirelessly tryin
 g to win the affection of grunge-rocker Cliff Poncier (Matt Dillon). as w
 ell as their neighbor Debbie Hunt (Sheila Kelly)\, who is aching for a hu
 sband who appreciates her and her fantastic earrings. The film also featu
 res an endless stream of stellar cameos\, including Eric Stoltz\, Bill Pu
 llman\, Tom Skerritt\, Peter Horton\, Tim Burton\, Eddie Vedder\, and so 
 many more! And\, of course\, the soundtrack is a who's who of grunge gods
 : Pearl Jam\, Mother Love Bone\, Soundgarden\, Alice in Chains\, and Mudh
 oney\, rounded out with the likes of The Smashing Pumpkins\, The Screamin
 g Trees\, and Paul Westerberg. [99 min\; comedy\, drama\, romance\; Engli
 sh]
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Arranged as an episodic comedy\, <i>Sin
 gles</i> spotlights the intertwined lives of the co-habitants\, friends\,
  and bandmates of the same Seattle apartment building. Foregrounded by th
 e tumultuous romantic relationship between Steve (Campbell Scott) and Lin
 da (Kyra Sedgwick)—who meet at an Alice in Chains concert\, of course!�
 ��the drama extends to their friendship with Janet Livermore (Bridget Fon
 da)\, who is tirelessly trying to win the affection of grunge-rocker Clif
 f Poncier (Matt Dillon). as well as their neighbor Debbie Hunt (Sheila Ke
 lly)\, who is aching for a husband who appreciates her and her fantastic 
 earrings. The film also features an endless stream of stellar cameos\, in
 cluding Eric Stoltz\, Bill Pullman\, Tom Skerritt\, Peter Horton\, Tim Bu
 rton\, Eddie Vedder\, and so many more! And\, of course\, the soundtrack 
 is a who's who of grunge gods: Pearl Jam\, Mother Love Bone\, Soundgarden
 \, Alice in Chains\, and Mudhoney\, rounded out with the likes of The Sma
 shing Pumpkins\, The Screaming Trees\, and Paul Westerberg. [99 min\; com
 edy\, drama\, romance\; English]</p>
