SUMMARY:House Party (1990) | Soundtracks of a Generation
DESCRIPTION:When Kid's father (Robin Harris) forbids him from attending P
 lay's (Christopher Martin) party\, Kid (Christopher Reid) sneaks out anyw
 ay\, kicking off a wild night full of dance-offs and rap battles\, run-in
 s with bullies and cops\, and a bit of romance. With an ensemble cast tha
 t also includes Tisha Campbell\, AJ Johnson\, Martin Lawrence\, Daryl "Ch
 ill" Mitchell\, and members of the music group Full Force\, plus a stella
 r soundtrack\, House Party is a beloved\, feel-good snapshot of early-199
 0s hip-hop culture that brought Black teenage experience to the mainstrea
 m. The breakthrough feature debut by writer-director Reginald Hudlin\, Ho
 use Party debuted to critical acclaim at the 1990 Sundance Film Festival.
  While some of its comedy certainly has not aged well\, House Party's sou
 ndtrack remains as fresh as the day it dropped. [100 min\; comedy\, music
 \; English]
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  When Kid's father (Robin Harris) forbid
 s him from attending Play's (Christopher Martin) party\, Kid (Christopher
  Reid) sneaks out anyway\, kicking off a wild night full of dance-offs an
 d rap battles\, run-ins with bullies and cops\, and a bit of romance. Wit
 h an ensemble cast that also includes Tisha Campbell\, AJ Johnson\, Marti
 n Lawrence\, Daryl "Chill" Mitchell\, and members of the music group Full
  Force\, plus a stellar soundtrack\, <i>House Party</i> is a beloved\, fe
 el-good snapshot of early-1990s hip-hop culture that brought Black teenag
 e experience to the mainstream. The breakthrough feature debut by writer-
 director Reginald Hudlin\, <i>House Party</i> debuted to critical acclaim
  at the 1990 Sundance Film Festival. While some of its comedy certainly h
 as not aged well\, <i>House Party</i>'s soundtrack remains as fresh as th
 e day it dropped. [100 min\; comedy\, music\; English]</p>
